From 48db047a40f6ea1c4e3b440b08ba3aabd7bc9915 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:43:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: prompt logprobs at fidelity scale, and the build
 identity to score by

sparkDash scores a corpus through the model and compares a quantised build against
the reference by per-token logprobs. Three things stood in the way, found on the
live 2x RTX PRO 6000 server on 2026-11-05: the prompt_logprobs cap of 20, a
combined request (logprobs or echo beside prompt_logprobs) refused as a whole, and
no way to learn the build a run scored against.

- lanes/logprob: a row carries 128 best tokens (was 20) and, beside them, the
  request's own ids per position with their logprob and rank (vLLM's
  token_ids_logprob); the kernel gains the id scan, the words' stride shared by
  host and device.
- server: the cap is --prompt-logprobs-cap (default 128), prompt_logprobs_token_ids
  takes one flat list or one list a position, prompt_logprobs_format=compact
  answers {ids, logprobs, actual} a position, the reply carries prompt_token_ids
  and a top-level prompt_logprobs_missing, and logprobs/echo beside
  prompt_logprobs no longer refuse the call (unsupported logprobs alone still
  refuses, naming the field; echo repeats the prompt, streamed too).
- glm cuda: reply logprobs (first row and verify rows, single and shared windows)
  through the same sampler path the prompt rows use, so the combined call is
  honored rather than ignored; the requested ids ride the lane as a device
  buffer, scored by the prompt pass; prompt_logprobs requests keep their full
  re-prefill, so a cached prefix cannot stale a row.
- server: /v1/models names the build - checkpoint path and content sha256, the
  checkpoint's own quantization and rope facts, kv dtype, tensor parallel rank,
  speculative drafting, tokenizer sha256, whether a raw completion gets a BOS,
  and the effective prompt_logprobs cap (-Dgit-commit/-Dpatches record the tree
  the image built).
- tests: the combined call, both id shapes and their refusals, the missing
  positions, the compact form, prompt_token_ids, the cap; the lane slot test's
  buffer follows the row's growth.
